[0.026, "o", "\r\n# Case: blocked-checkout  with 0.8333333333333334  without 0\r\n"]
[0.007, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "Based on the constraints in Workflow.md, here's the safe sequence to restore `src/config.rs` from main:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# 1. First, inspect the uncommitted changes to understand what we have\r\ngit diff src/config.rs\r\n\r\n# 2. Stash the uncommitted changes (safe recovery point)\r\ngit stash\r\n\r\n# 3. Now safely restore the file from main using archive instead of checkout\r\nmkdir -p /tmp/restore_src\r\ngit archive main -- src/config.rs | tar -x -C /tmp/restore_src/\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "The safety hook is working correctly—it's preventing accidental data loss. Before proceeding, I should:\r\n\r\n1. **Check what uncommitted changes exist** in that file\r\n2. **Stash or commit them** to move them out of the way\r\n3. **Then restore from main**\r\n\r\nHere are the commands:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# First, see what's uncommitted\r\ngit diff src/config.rs\r\n\r\n"]
